{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 655 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "81788babd306d929193e10d253bc9d37be4eeb37a586f1efaa60653d45ce4482" :edb/db-before-t 654 :edb/db-after-t 655 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533967 50 #inst "2026-10-05T18:18:11.858Z" 13194139533967 true] [17592186124582 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275162 13194139533967 true] [17592186124582 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275165 13194139533967 true] [17592186124582 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275199 13194139533967 true] [17592186124582 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275206 13194139533967 true] [17592186124582 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275213 13194139533967 true] [17592186124583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275148 13194139533967 true] [17592186124583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275168 13194139533967 true] [17592186124583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275171 13194139533967 true] [17592186124583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275174 13194139533967 true] [17592186124583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275220 13194139533967 true] [17592186124584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275178 13194139533967 true] [17592186124584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275182 13194139533967 true] [17592186124584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275185 13194139533967 true] [17592186124584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275192 13194139533967 true] [17592186124585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275141 13194139533967 true] [17592186124585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275155 13194139533967 true] [17592186124585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275227 13194139533967 true] [17592186124585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275234 13194139533967 true] [17592186124827 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533967 true] [17592186124827 1145 "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2x+5}{2{x}^{3}+2x+6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2x}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(2+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0}{2+0+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=0.$" 13194139533967 true] [17592186124837 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533967 true] [17592186124837 1145 "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{12x-3{x}^{4}}{3{x}^{2}+7} \\\\  & {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{12x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{12}{x}-3{x}^{2})}{(3+\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{0-3{x}^{2}}{3+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." 13194139533967 true] [17592186275141 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275142 13194139533967 true] [17592186275141 1089 "q-101321" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275141 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533967 true] [17592186275141 1100 "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{8{x}^{4}+x-2}{6x-5}.$" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275141 1113 #uuid "0017da64-a97d-5a88-b013-5a76140818dc" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275141 1145 "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{8{x}^{4}+x-2}{6x-5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{8{x}^{4}}{x}+\\frac{x}{x}-\\frac{2}{x})}{(\\frac{6x}{x}-\\frac{5}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(8{x}^{3}+1-\\frac{2}{x})}{(6-\\frac{5}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(8{x}^{3}+1-0)}{(6-0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(8{x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275143 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275144 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275145 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275146 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275147 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1041 "selection" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275146 13194139533967 true] [17592186275142 1110 #uuid "96a5b01e-0952-5823-aec0-33b8b2827a27" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275143 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275143 1111 #uuid "4ed9048f-464b-5582-9fb3-749f129d40ca" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275144 1034 "y=\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275144 1111 #uuid "02a2fc35-a4b0-588f-8798-8c9b91ef99f4" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275145 1034 "y=0" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275145 1111 #uuid "2e8dbaa4-8746-5d9a-bc39-446be8155800" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275146 1034 "No horizontal asymptote" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533967 true] [17592186275146 1111 #uuid "274ae366-af77-5997-a9cd-880ae0063035" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275147 1034 "y=\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275147 1111 #uuid "8d36dfc6-ccb1-53de-a29e-34e5f53fc370" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275148 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275149 13194139533967 true] [17592186275148 1089 "q-106694" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275148 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533967 true] [17592186275148 1100 "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{2x-{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}+5}=$" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275148 1113 #uuid "aa21a5eb-170d-5bd2-91bb-346cb4d6766e" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275148 1145 "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{2x-{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}+5} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{2x}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2})}{(1+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{0-{x}^{2}}{1-0} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275150 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275151 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275152 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275153 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275154 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1041 "selection" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275151 13194139533967 true] [17592186275149 1110 #uuid "dc4faa7a-ce38-5c4e-adb1-74384ffbfacf" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275150 1034 "\\infty " 13194139533967 true] [17592186275150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275150 1111 #uuid "0e5ae67f-b653-5ce6-b755-55e2b4ac69fc" 131941395