nite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275157 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275158 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275159 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275160 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275161 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1041 "selection" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275159 13194139533967 true] [17592186275156 1110 #uuid "7bf9256b-03e8-5ac3-88fd-10615dd8ed9a" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275157 1034 "y=\\frac{11}{2}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275157 1111 #uuid "6d289c4d-66f9-5bc3-ba56-6f40a3dd4628" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275158 1034 "y=-\\frac{11}{2}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275158 1111 #uuid "57140c10-c243-59a6-a36d-d4ee1187cf49" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275159 1034 "No horizontal asymptote" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533967 true] [17592186275159 1111 #uuid "eec3b875-66a9-5dff-878d-62bcc4f5aad1" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275160 1034 "y=2" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275160 1111 #uuid "938099ab-6674-5275-bf78-41bf3fd9fe1d" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275161 1034 "-2" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275161 1111 #uuid "1fd6c2f5-fa61-51d4-8143-2a3ff0cb7e38" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275162 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275163 13194139533967 true] [17592186275162 1089 "q-339421" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275162 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533967 true] [17592186275162 1100 "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2}{4{x}^{6}-5x}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275162 1113 #uuid "a921d240-c753-5086-9f3e-3453deca86b6" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275162 1145 "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{6}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2}{4{x}^{6}-5x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{6}})}{(\\frac{4{x}^{6}}{{x}^{6}}-\\frac{5x}{{x}^{6}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{6}})}{(4-\\frac{5}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{4-0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275164 13194139533967 true] [17592186275163 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533967 true] [17592186275163 1041 "field-1" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275163 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275164 13194139533967 true] [17592186275163 1110 #uuid "286f59c2-1895-5098-9962-872de30b9e95" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275164 1034 "0" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275164 1111 #uuid "d6f8e3ec-a75e-53fe-b29a-1366c55b7a1b" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275165 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275166 13194139533967 true] [17592186275165 1089 "q-339507" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275165 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533967 true] [17592186275165 1100 "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{|-12x+5|}{4x+3}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275165 1113 #uuid "000da502-b1b5-5116-a1b7-f93b9f904ead" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275165 1145 "For large negative values of $x,$ we have $|-12x+5|=-12x+5.$ Consequently, for $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{|-12x+5|}{4x+3}=\\frac{-12x+5}{4x+3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{1}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-12x+5}{4x+3} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{-12x}{x}+\\frac{5}{x})}{(\\frac{4x}{x}+\\frac{3}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(-12+\\frac{5}{x})}{(4+\\frac{3}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12+0}{4+0} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275167 13194139533967 true] [17592186275166 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533967 true] [17592186275166 1041 "field-1" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275166 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275167 13194139533967 true] [17592186275166 1110 #uuid "53891a93-adff-583b-ad1e-85c1380df81f" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275167 1034 "-3" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275167 1111 #uuid "4b99e024-0827-5449-bdf4-75125c45a836" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275168 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275169 13194139533967 true] [17592186275168 1089 "q-339612" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275168 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533967 true] [17592186275168 1100 "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{-{x}^{6}+4x}{{x}^{2}+x+5}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275168 1113 #uuid "4c34786e-7329-5ee5-938e-61e317be395c" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275168 1145 "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{-{x}^{6}+4x}{{x}^{2}+5} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{-{x}^{6}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(-{x}^{4}+\\frac{4}{x})}{(1+\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(-{x}^{4}+0)}{(1+0)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,-{x}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275169 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275170 13194139533967 true] [17592186275169 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533967 true] [17592186275169 1041 "field-1" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275169 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275170 13194139533967 true] [17592186275169 1110 #uuid "59067eab-dbc9-5efb-a806-44544690b377" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275170 1034 "-\\infty" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533967 true] [17592186275170 1111 #uuid "74885b07-6eb9-512f-88de-44f3f84c5a50" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275171 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275172 13194139533967 true] [17592186275171 1089 "q-339621" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275171 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533967 true] [17592186275171 1100 "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{-{x}^{9}-6{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{3}+10x}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275171 1113 #uuid "3bcb15bd-9c0c-5c65-97b9-07fcb59a2733" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275171 1145 "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{-{x}^{9}-6{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{3}+10x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{-{x}^{9}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{10x}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(-{x}^{6}-\\frac{6}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(1+\\frac{10}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\text{ }\\frac{-{x}^{6}-0+0}{1+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,-{x}^{6} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533967 true] [17592186275172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275173 13194139533967 true] [17592186275172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533967 tru